  3. [1mDOM layer[0m: [38;5;153mshowErrors(formEl, errors)[39m, [38;5;153mclearErrors(formEl)[39m, and the one function forms actually call:
     [38;5;153mvalidateForm(formEl, schema) → { valid, values, errors }[39m — reads the field values, validates, renders errors, hands
     back the result.

  [38;5;153mapp.js[39m keeps its own submit listener (per your boundary choice, the module doesn't touch submit):

  [34mimport[39m { validateForm, required, minLength, email } [34mfrom[39m [31m"./validation.mjs"[39m;

  [34mconst[39m loginSchema = {
    [36musername[39m: [[33mrequired[39m(), [33mminLength[39m([32m3[39m)],
    [36mpassword[39m: [[33mrequired[39m(), [33mminLength[39m([32m8[39m)],
  };

  document.[33mgetElementById[39m([31m"login-form"[39m).[33maddEventListener[39m([31m"submit"[39m, [33m([39me) => {
    e.[33mpreventDefault[39m();
    [34mconst[39m { valid, values } = [33mvalidateForm[39m(e.target, loginSchema);
    [34mif[39m (!valid) [34mreturn[39m;
