  [38;5;153mvalidateForm[39m returning [38;5;153mvalues[39m means the handler never does [38;5;153mgetElementById[39m again — that's the duplication that would
  otherwise grow with every new form.

  [1mWhy [38;5;153m.mjs[39m and not [38;5;153m.js[39m.[0m There's a snag worth surfacing: [38;5;153mpackage.json[39m has no [38;5;153m"type"[39m field, so Node treats every [38;5;153m.js[39m file
  as CommonJS. A [38;5;153mvalidation.js[39m using [38;5;153mexport[39m would work in the browser but fail to import in a Node test. The fixes are
  to set [38;5;153m"type": "module"[39m — which breaks [38;5;153msrc/index.js[39m and [38;5;153msrc/utils.js[39m, files unrelated to this work — or to use the
  [38;5;153m.mjs[39m extension, which Node always reads as ESM and browsers don't care about either way. I'm proposing [38;5;153m.mjs[39m to keep
  the change off the [38;5;153msrc/[39m tree. The cost is a one-off extension inconsistency next to [38;5;153mapp.js[39m.

  [1mFiles touched:[0m [38;5;153mvalidation.mjs[39m (new), [38;5;153mapp.js[39m (import the module, drop the local [38;5;153mvalidateForm[39m, read values from the
  returned object), [38;5;153mindex.html[39m ([38;5;153mname[39m attributes on the two inputs; [38;5;153m<script type="module" src="app.js">[39m).

  Does the API shape and the [38;5;153m.mjs[39m call look right before I move on to the rendering and error-handling section?

